{
  "duration": 147.516375,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.06,
      "text": "You now know how to use AI, and because you understand the engine underneath,"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.6,
      "end": 7.66,
      "text": "its strange behavior actually makes sense."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.36,
      "end": 10.66,
      "text": "Your primary goal was to be smarter than the tool."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.32,
      "end": 11.46,
      "text": "Done."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.4,
      "end": 15.42,
      "text": "But now comes the question almost everyone is arguing about."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.04,
      "end": 21.96,
      "text": "Now that we control the tool, where does this entire technological shift actually land for society?"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.78,
      "end": 24.44,
      "text": "You have probably heard the voices already."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.0,
      "end": 27.32,
      "text": "People are deeply divided on what happens next."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.0,
      "end": 32.68,
      "text": "You likely know an AI optimist who thinks this technology is amazing, fantastic,"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.12,
      "end": 35.2,
      "text": "and every other superlative they can string together."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.82,
      "end": 40.12,
      "text": "You also know an AI warrior who is absolutely certain it will hurt society."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.0,
      "end": 41.78,
      "text": "Here's the honest part."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.54,
      "end": 43.0,
      "text": "Nobody knows."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.68,
      "end": 49.76,
      "text": "Not the optimists, not the worriers, not us, and not even the engineers actively building the AI."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.9,
      "end": 51.9,
      "text": "Think back to history class."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.76,
      "end": 55.44,
      "text": "Centuries ago, map makers had to deal with a similar problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.0,
      "end": 60.78,
      "text": "They sometimes filled waters they did not understand with sea monsters and strange serpents."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.64,
      "end": 64.86,
      "text": "The future of AI is like the unknown ocean on those old maps."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.8,
      "end": 70.34,
      "text": "The AI warriors filled these uncharted spaces with AI monsters that destroy jobs,"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.7,
      "end": 72.0,
      "text": "hack systems, and take over."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.72,
      "end": 77.82,
      "text": "AI optimists look at the exact sampling space and see easy, clear sailing through open water."
    },
    {
      "start": 78.52,
      "end": 81.42,
      "text": "But those historical sailors didn't actually find sea monsters,"
    },
    {
      "start": 81.72,
      "end": 84.18,
      "text": "and they rarely found easy, clear sailing either."
    },
    {
      "start": 84.18,
      "end": 87.42,
      "text": "They usually found something entirely unexpected."
    },
    {
      "start": 88.64,
      "end": 92.24,
      "text": "As we move forward, we have to take both views of the map seriously."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.0,
      "end": 96.24,
      "text": "The potential for monsters and the promise of open water."
    },
    {
      "start": 97.24,
      "end": 99.38,
      "text": "Only one thing is certain in all of this."
    },
    {
      "start": 99.92,
      "end": 101.3,
      "text": "AI is here to stay."
    },
    {
      "start": 101.98,
      "end": 106.12,
      "text": "That doesn't mean it keeps getting better endlessly, it just means it isn't going away."
    },
    {
      "start": 107.0,
      "end": 112.96,
      "text": "Since it is a permanent fixture, our best approach is to ask the right questions before we map the territory."
    },
    {
      "start": 113.68,
      "end": 117.92,
      "text": "This section provides a toolset designed to help you answer three critical questions."
    },
    {
      "start": 119.04,
      "end": 122.2,
      "text": "First, why do people disagree so much about AI's future?"
    },
    {
      "start": 123.22,
      "end": 127.46,
      "text": "Second, what could AI do to make society better, and where could it go wrong?"
    },
    {
      "start": 128.18,
      "end": 131.64,
      "text": "And third, how could AI change my future life and work?"
    },
    {
      "start": 132.44,
      "end": 135.38,
      "text": "Right now, these questions are completely unanswered."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.9,
      "end": 138.96,
      "text": "They are the only compass we have before stepping into the unknown."
    },
    {
      "start": 139.84,
      "end": 141.22,
      "text": "Nobody has a map of what's coming."
    },
    {
      "start": 141.22,
      "end": 143.9,
      "text": "You're ready to sail into the blank space."
    }
  ],
